==German==

===Etymology===
Old High German ''tōden'', originally *''dōden'', compare Old Norse {{term|deyða}} (> Danish {{term|døde|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|döda|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌳𐌰𐌿𐌸𐌾𐌰𐌽|tr=dauþjan|sc=Goth}} and Dutch [[doden]].

